# Neo Wave parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoWave
namespace NeoBuzz.Wave
class NeoWaveMachine
tracks 16
summary Wavetable synth: two table oscillators with warps, sub and noise, a filter, three envelopes, two LFOs and a mod matrix; loads WAV wavetables. Use it for evolving pads, digital leads and modern basses.
import wavetable .wav | A WAV wavetable: frames of 2048 samples (or a clm chunk saying the frame size), or one short single cycle. Becomes the "User" table (A table or B table = User).

group Voice
VoiceMode   "Voice mode"    0 2    0    enum Poly Mono Legato           | Poly; Mono retriggers; Legato glides without retriggering
    how Chooses how notes share voices: Poly plays chords, Mono retriggers on each note, Legato glides between overlapping notes.
    sound Poly suits pads and chords, Mono gives a punchy lead or bass line, and Legato gives smooth, connected phrases.
Polyphony   "Polyphony"     1 16   8    int 0                           | Notes that sound at once
    how Sets how many notes can sound at once, from 1 to 16.
    sound More voices let chords and long releases overlap, while fewer save processing power and make notes cut each other off.
Unison      "Unison"        1 8    1    int 0                           | Voices per note
    how Sets the number of stacked voices per note, from 1 to 8.
    sound More voices make the note thicker and wider, and one voice is a single clean oscillator.
UniDetune   "Uni detune"    0 1000 200  pct                             | Detune between unison voices (up to ±50 cents)
    how Sets how far apart the unison voices are tuned, up to 50 cents.
    sound Small amounts give a warm thickness and large ones a wide, swarming supersaw sound.
UniSpread   "Uni spread"    0 1000 600  pct                             | Stereo spread of unison voices
    how Sets how widely the unison voices are spread across the stereo field, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More spread makes the note wider and more enveloping, and zero keeps it centred.
GlideMode   "Glide mode"    0 2    0    enum Off Always Legato          | When notes glide
    how Chooses when notes slide into each other: never, always, or only on overlapping notes.
    sound Gliding adds a singing, synth-bass slur between notes.
Glide       "Glide"         0 1000 200  pow 0 2 3 s 3                   | Glide time
    how Sets how long the slide takes, up to 2 seconds.
    sound Short glides are subtle and long ones sweep slowly between pitches.
BendRange   "Bend range"    0 24   2    int 0 st                        | Pitch bend range
    how Sets how far the pitch bend wheel moves the pitch, from 0 to 24 semitones.
    sound A small range gives expressive nudges, and a large one gives dive-bomb sweeps.
Volume      "Volume"        0 1000 739  db -40 6 inf                    | Output level
    how Sets the output level of the synth, from -40 to +6 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to place the instrument in the mix without changing its tone.
VelAmp      "Vel → amp"     0 1000 700  pct                             | How much velocity changes loudness
    how Sets how strongly note velocity changes the loudness, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound High values make playing dynamics audible, and 0 % makes all notes equally loud.

group Osc A
ATable    "A table"     0 10   0 enum Basic PWM Harmonics Formants Sync_sweep FM_sweep Organ Resonant Digital Grit User | Wavetable (User: the table loaded in the editor)
    how Chooses the wavetable for oscillator A, from the built-in sets or the loaded User table.
    sound Each table has its own family of tones, from basic shapes to vowels, sweeping sync and gritty digital sounds.
APos      "A position"  0 1000 0 pct | Position in the table (frames morph smoothly)
    how Moves through the frames of oscillator A's wavetable, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the position morphs the tone smoothly from one timbre to the next, and modulating it makes evolving sounds.
AWarp     "A warp"      0 7    0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Window_sync PM_from_B | How the cycle is read
    how Chooses how the cycle of oscillator A is bent or read: bend, squeeze, mirror, asymmetry, window sync or phase modulation.
    sound Each warp reshapes the waveform and adds harmonics, from subtle fattening to hard, metallic edges.
AWarpAmt  "A warp amt"  0 1000 0    pct | Warp amount
    how Sets how strongly the warp is applied to oscillator A, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Zero leaves the table untouched, and more warp makes the tone progressively more extreme.
AOct      "A octave"    0 6    3    int -3 oct signed | Octave
    how Transposes oscillator A up or down by up to three octaves.
    sound Lower octaves give weight and higher ones brightness or a thin layer.
ASemi     "A semi"      0 24   12   int -12 st signed | Semitones
    how Transposes oscillator A by up to 12 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to build intervals and chords from the two oscillators, such as a fifth.
AFine     "A fine"      0 1000 500  lin -50 50 ct 0 | Fine tune
    how Detunes oscillator A by up to 50 cents either way.
    sound A few cents between the oscillators gives a slow, warm beating.
ALevel    "A level"     0 1000 1000 pct | Level
    how Sets the level of oscillator A into the filter, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Use it to balance the two oscillators against each other.
group Osc B
BTable    "B table"     0 10   3 enum Basic PWM Harmonics Formants Sync_sweep FM_sweep Organ Resonant Digital Grit User | Wavetable (User: the table loaded in the editor)
    how Chooses the wavetable for oscillator B, from the built-in sets or the loaded User table.
    sound Each table has its own family of tones, from basic shapes to vowels, sweeping sync and gritty digital sounds.
BPos      "B position"  0 1000 0 pct | Position in the table (frames morph smoothly)
    how Moves through the frames of oscillator B's wavetable, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the position morphs the tone smoothly from one timbre to the next, and modulating it makes evolving sounds.
BWarp     "B warp"      0 7    0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Window_sync PM_from_B | How the cycle is read (PM from B acts on osc A only; here it reads plainly)
    how Chooses how the cycle of oscillator B is bent or read: bend, squeeze, mirror, asymmetry, window sync or phase modulation.
    sound Each warp reshapes the waveform and adds harmonics, from subtle fattening to hard, metallic edges.
BWarpAmt  "B warp amt"  0 1000 0    pct | Warp amount
    how Sets how strongly the warp is applied to oscillator B, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Zero leaves the table untouched, and more warp makes the tone progressively more extreme.
BOct      "B octave"    0 6    3    int -3 oct signed | Octave
    how Transposes oscillator B up or down by up to three octaves.
    sound Lower octaves give weight and higher ones brightness or a thin layer.
BSemi     "B semi"      0 24   12   int -12 st signed | Semitones
    how Transposes oscillator B by up to 12 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to build intervals and chords from the two oscillators, such as a fifth.
BFine     "B fine"      0 1000 540  lin -50 50 ct 0 | Fine tune
    how Detunes oscillator B by up to 50 cents either way.
    sound A few cents between the oscillators gives a slow, warm beating.
BLevel    "B level"     0 1000 0 pct | Level
    how Sets the level of oscillator B into the filter, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Use it to balance the two oscillators against each other.

group Sub · noise
SubShape    "Sub shape"     0 1    0    enum Sine Square                | Sub oscillator wave
    how Chooses a sine or a square wave for the sub oscillator.
    sound Sine gives a smooth, deep foundation and square a more audible, buzzy bass.
SubOct      "Sub octave"    0 1    0    enum -1 -2                      | Octaves below the note
    how Chooses whether the sub oscillator sits one or two octaves below the note.
    sound One octave down adds weight and two octaves down adds a rumble.
SubLevel    "Sub level"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Sub level
    how Sets the level of the sub oscillator, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Raise it for more low-end weight in bass and lead sounds.
NoiseLevel  "Noise"         0 1000 0    pct                             | Noise level
    how Sets the level of the noise source, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A little adds air and breath, and a lot makes the sound hissy and percussive.

group Filter
FType       "Filter type"   0 6    0    enum Ladder_24 Ladder_12 SVF_LP SVF_BP SVF_HP SVF_Notch Off | Filter model
    how Chooses the filter model: 24 or 12 dB ladder, state-variable low-pass, band-pass, high-pass or notch, or off.
    sound The ladder is warm and smooth, the state-variable types are cleaner and more flexible, and Off leaves the oscillators open.
FCutoff     "Cutoff"        0 1000 750  freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
    how Sets the filter cutoff frequency, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz.
    sound Low values make the sound dark and muffled, and high values open it up and brighten it.
FReso       "Reso"          0 1000 150  pct                             | Resonance
    how Sets the filter resonance, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More resonance puts a whistling peak at the cutoff, and a lot makes it ring.
FDrive      "Drive"         0 1000 0    lin 0 24 dB 1                   | Drive into the filter
    how Pushes the signal into the filter by up to 24 dB.
    sound A little adds warmth and a lot makes the sound thick and distorted.
FEnv        "Filter env"    0 1000 600  bip                             | Filter envelope amount (±6 octaves)
    how Sets how much the filter envelope moves the cutoff, up to six octaves either way.
    sound Positive amounts make each note open and close, and negative ones sweep the other way.
FKey        "Key track"     0 1000 500  pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard
    how Sets how much the cutoff follows the note pitch, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 100 % the brightness stays the same over the keyboard, and lower values make high notes duller.
FVel        "Filter vel"    0 1000 300  pct                             | Softer notes close the filter (up to 3 octaves)
    how Sets how much soft notes close the filter, up to three octaves.
    sound Harder playing sounds brighter, which makes the instrument feel more expressive.

group Amp env
AmpA        "Amp attack"    0 1000 100  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets how long the amp envelope takes to rise from nothing to full, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short attacks hit instantly for plucks and basses, and long ones fade in slowly like a pad.
AmpD        "Amp decay"     0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets how long the amp envelope takes to fall to its sustain level, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short decays give a plucky, percussive note, and long ones let the note ring down slowly.
AmpS        "Amp sustain"   0 1000 800  pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the level the amp envelope holds while the key stays down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A low sustain makes the note die away even when held, and a high one keeps it at full volume.
AmpR        "Amp release"   0 1000 450  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets how long the amp envelope takes to fall back after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short releases stop the note cleanly, and long ones let it fade out after you let go.
group Filter env
FltA        "Flt attack"    0 1000 100  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to rise from nothing to full, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short attacks open at once, and long ones make the effect swell in after the note starts.
FltD        "Flt decay"     0 1000 520  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to fall to its sustain level, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short decays make a quick snap in the effect, and long ones a slow, gradual sweep down.
FltS        "Flt sustain"   0 1000 300  pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the level the filter envelope holds while the key stays down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A high sustain keeps the effect on while the key is held, and a low one lets it fade back.
FltR        "Flt release"   0 1000 450  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to fall back after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short releases end the effect at once, and long ones let it tail off after the note.
group Mod env
ModA        "Mod attack"    0 1000 300  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets how long the mod envelope takes to rise from nothing to full, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short attacks open at once, and long ones make the effect swell in after the note starts.
ModD        "Mod decay"     0 1000 600  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets how long the mod envelope takes to fall to its sustain level, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short decays make a quick snap in the effect, and long ones a slow, gradual sweep down.
ModS        "Mod sustain"   0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the level the mod envelope holds while the key stays down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A high sustain keeps the effect on while the key is held, and a low one lets it fade back.
ModR        "Mod release"   0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets how long the mod envelope takes to fall back after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short releases end the effect at once, and long ones let it tail off after the note.

group LFO 1
L1Shape     "LFO1 shape"    0 6    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth | Waveform
    how Chooses the waveform of LFO 1: sine, triangle, rising or falling saw, square, random steps or smooth random.
    sound Smooth shapes give gentle sweeps, square gives on-off jumps, and random shapes give unpredictable movement.
L1Rate      "LFO1 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
    how Sets the speed of LFO 1 from 0.02 to 50 Hz when its sync is Free.
    sound Slow rates drift over seconds, and fast rates turn into vibrato and tremolo.
L1Sync      "LFO1 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
    how Locks LFO 1 to a note length of the song tempo instead of the Rate control.
    sound Synced modulation moves in time with the track.
L1Retrig    "LFO1 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (per voice); off: one free LFO
    how Chooses whether LFO 1 restarts with each note or runs freely.
    sound Restarting gives every note the same movement, and free running makes each note slightly different.
L1Fade      "LFO1 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
    how Sets how long LFO 1 takes to fade in after a note starts, up to 5 seconds.
    sound A fade delays vibrato or sweeps until the note has settled, as a player would add vibrato late.
group LFO 2
L2Shape     "LFO2 shape"    0 6    1    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth | Waveform
    how Chooses the waveform of LFO 2: sine, triangle, rising or falling saw, square, random steps or smooth random.
    sound Smooth shapes give gentle sweeps, square gives on-off jumps, and random shapes give unpredictable movement.
L2Rate      "LFO2 rate"     0 1000 300  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
    how Sets the speed of LFO 2 from 0.02 to 50 Hz when its sync is Free.
    sound Slow rates drift over seconds, and fast rates turn into vibrato and tremolo.
L2Sync      "LFO2 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
    how Locks LFO 2 to a note length of the song tempo instead of the Rate control.
    sound Synced modulation moves in time with the track.
L2Retrig    "LFO2 retrig"   0 1    0    switch                          | Restart with each note (per voice); off: one free LFO
    how Chooses whether LFO 2 restarts with each note or runs freely.
    sound Restarting gives every note the same movement, and free running makes each note slightly different.
L2Fade      "LFO2 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
    how Sets how long LFO 2 takes to fade in after a note starts, up to 5 seconds.
    sound A fade delays vibrato or sweeps until the note has settled, as a player would add vibrato late.

group Matrix
M1Src "M1 source" 0 11 1 enum Off LFO_1 LFO_2 Mod_env Filter_env Amp_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Random Unison | Modulation source
    how Chooses what drives matrix slot 1, such as an LFO, an envelope, velocity or the mod wheel.
    sound The source decides how the destination moves: steadily, with the note, or with your playing.
M1Dst "M1 dest"   0 17 0 enum Off Pitch A_pitch B_pitch A_position B_position A_warp B_warp A_level B_level Sub_level Noise_level Cutoff Reso Amp Pan LFO_1_rate LFO_2_rate | Modulation destination
    how Chooses which control matrix slot 1 moves.
    sound Pointing a source at pitch, filter, level or pan changes what the movement does to the sound.
M1Amt "M1 amount" 0 1000 500 bip | Amount
    how Sets how strongly slot 1 moves its destination, from minus 100 % to plus 100 %.
    sound Positive values push the destination up, negative values push it down, and zero does nothing.
M2Src "M2 source" 0 11 8 enum Off LFO_1 LFO_2 Mod_env Filter_env Amp_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Random Unison | Modulation source
    how Chooses what drives matrix slot 2, such as an LFO, an envelope, velocity or the mod wheel.
    sound The source decides how the destination moves: steadily, with the note, or with your playing.
M2Dst "M2 dest"   0 17 0 enum Off Pitch A_pitch B_pitch A_position B_position A_warp B_warp A_level B_level Sub_level Noise_level Cutoff Reso Amp Pan LFO_1_rate LFO_2_rate | Modulation destination
    how Chooses which control matrix slot 2 moves.
    sound Pointing a source at pitch, filter, level or pan changes what the movement does to the sound.
M2Amt "M2 amount" 0 1000 500 bip | Amount
    how Sets how strongly slot 2 moves its destination, from minus 100 % to plus 100 %.
    sound Positive values push the destination up, negative values push it down, and zero does nothing.
M3Src "M3 source" 0 11 3 enum Off LFO_1 LFO_2 Mod_env Filter_env Amp_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Random Unison | Modulation source
    how Chooses what drives matrix slot 3, such as an LFO, an envelope, velocity or the mod wheel.
    sound The source decides how the destination moves: steadily, with the note, or with your playing.
